# The hollow choir, seen for the first time. Fired by proximity + line of
# sight (CompProperties_TSC_ProximityDialogue on TSC_ChoirBones), once per
# save. The check spot's own options - sing, read, shove - are the follow-up;
# this is only the noticing.

dialogue TSC_Dialogue_ChoirSight

# The party can reach the bones AFTER settling the cantor (either way):
# then "someone below is singing" would be nonsense - the recital is over.
entry known if flag(TSC_CantorRested)
entry known if flag(TSC_CantorFought)

== start ==
The lamplight finds them all at once: skulls, stacked rank on rank from flagstone to roof, filling the gallery wall ahead.

They are not piled. They are placed - every one of them set level, every one of them facing the same way, down the passage toward the deep floor. Whoever arranged this did it slowly, and meant it.

Nobody says anything for a moment. Under the drip of the cistern water, very faint, the sound that has followed you since the stairs is still there: someone below, singing.

* "They're facing the singing." -> facing
* "Wren. Tell me this is ordinary ossuary work." -> wren
    if in_party(TSC_Npc_Bard)
* [Move on.] -> end

== facing ==
Once it is said, it cannot be unseen: eight hundred years of the dead seated in congregation, all of them turned toward the voice on the floor below.

Not a burial. An audience. Somebody wanted the dead to hear.

* [Move on.] -> end
    do grant_xp(10)

== wren ==
Wren does not answer at once. Her eyes move along the rows like a page, and under the dread there is an awful, professional delight fighting to get out.

"Ossuaries face the dead east, toward the morning. These face *down*." She steps closer instead of back. "And look - the rows! Long, long, short. Do you see it? They're not stacked, they're *scored*. Somebody wrote the dead into the song. That's the most terrifying thing I've ever seen and part of me wants to applaud."

She pulls her cloak tighter, which does not stop her taking one more step.

"I'd like to meet whoever is still singing to them. And I'd like it very much to be on our terms."

* [Move on.] -> end
    do grant_xp(15); affinity(+5)

== known ==
The lamplight finds them all at once: skulls, stacked rank on rank from flagstone to roof, filling the gallery wall ahead.

They are not piled. They are placed - every one of them set level, every one of them facing the same way, down the passage toward the deep floor. Toward the chamber where the singing used to come from.

An audience in rows, kept for eight hundred years. The party has already met their singer. Whatever this recital was, it has had its last verse, and the dead are still leaning in to listen.

* [Move on.] -> end
    do grant_xp(10)
